  "awb---faq-data": "<div data-rt-embed-type='true'><div data-rt-embed-type='true'><script> window.awbFAQ = {\"heading\": \"Complaint Form Questions, Answered\", \"items\": [{\"q\": \"What is a complaint form?\", \"a\": \"A complaint form is a structured record of a grievance against a business or a public body. It captures what happened, in the complainant's words, and the outcome they want. Employers and city offices keep their own versions, each worded for the complaints that reach them.\"}, {\"q\": \"How do I make a complaint form online?\", \"a\": \"Start with the kinds of complaint you receive and the facts each one needs, then add a question about the outcome the person wants. Describe that to Emergent's <a href='https://emergent.sh/ai-form-builder'>AI form builder</a>. It builds the form with a numbered case for each complaint, plus a table that tracks every reply.\"}, {\"q\": \"What types of complaint forms are there?\", \"a\": \"Most complaint forms fall into four groups. Consumer complaints go to the business first and then, if that fails, to a state consumer protection office. Workplace complaints go to HR. Court complaints start a civil lawsuit, and state regulators take complaints about the businesses they oversee.\"}, {\"q\": \"What is a civil complaint form?\", \"a\": \"A civil complaint form is the document that starts a lawsuit. Filing it with the court opens the case, and the person filing becomes the plaintiff. Some state courts publish fill-in versions, such as California's form complaint for personal injury. Use the court's own form when filing there.\"}, {\"q\": \"What does a summons and complaint form include?\", \"a\": \"In federal court, the complaint sets out the claim and the relief the plaintiff asks for, along with why the court can hear the case. The clerk signs the summons, which names the parties and tells the defendant how long they have to respond. The plaintiff serves the two together, and a defendant who misses the deadline risks a default judgment.\"}, {\"q\": \"How do you keep track of complaint forms?\", \"a\": \"Give every submission a case number and one owner, and keep them all in one table instead of a shared inbox. Check the open cases each week, oldest first. With Emergent, the form and that table come from one prompt, and the table lives in a database you own.\"}, {\"q\": \"What should an online complaint form ask for?\", \"a\": \"Ask for contact details and a category, then a description and the outcome wanted. Customers also need an order or account number and a way to attach photos. An online complaint form should show a case number on screen, which the person can quote in any follow-up.\"}, {\"q\": \"Where should you send an employee complaint form?\", \"a\": \"Send it to HR or to the person the company's policy names, never to anyone the complaint is about. Give employees a second route for complaints about HR itself. On a web form, a routing rule can skip any manager the complaint names before that manager sees it.\"}, {\"q\": \"What fields does an employee complaint form need?\", \"a\": \"An employee complaint form asks who or what the complaint is about and when it happened, plus any witnesses. A free-text box for the full account matters more than any dropdown. If it describes an injury or a hazard, the facts belong on an incident report form too.\"}, {\"q\": \"Is there a free complaint form template?\", \"a\": \"Template galleries offer free starting points with the usual fields. A template has no routing or reply tracking, and Emergent, which is free to start, builds both from your description. Keep praise and ideas on a separate <a href='https://emergent.sh/ai-form-builder/feedback-form'>feedback form</a> so complaints stay easy to find.\"}]}; </script></div></div>"
 }
}